From: Dmitry Safonov <dima@arista.com>
Subject: [PATCH] perf/build: Include linux/string.h by jitdump.c for strlcpy()

The perf tools string header declares the built-in strlcpy() fallback when
the system C library predates glibc 2.38, as on Debian Bookworm.

Submitted upstream (not merged):
https://lore.kernel.org/lkml/20261126-perf-string-h-v1-1-8f5c39ff30f0@arista.com/
Message-ID: <20261126-perf-string-h-v1-1-8f5c39ff30f0@arista.com>
Signed-off-by: Dmitry Safonov <dima@arista.com>
[Shirube: use the exact Linux 6.6.163 diff context.]

--- a/tools/perf/util/jitdump.c
+++ b/tools/perf/util/jitdump.c
@@ -5,7 +5,7 @@
 #include <libgen.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
-#include <string.h>
+#include <linux/string.h>
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
 #include <inttypes.h>
